<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 40 40" role="img" aria-label="Language Babe">
  <!--
    The installed app's icon: the same speech bubble as the header lockup, and
    the third hand-written copy of it — the other two are
    `resources/views/components/brand_mark.edge` and
    `inertia/components/brand_mark.tsx`. It cannot import either, because a
    manifest icon is fetched as a standalone document with no stylesheet, so
    the two palette variables the components use are spelled out as hex here.
    If the mark changes, all three change.

    A full-bleed rounded rect rather than a transparent glyph: Android masks
    this into whatever shape the launcher uses, and a transparent icon gets
    masked into a floating fragment.
  -->
  <rect width="40" height="40" rx="11" fill="#6d4ae6" />
  <path
    d="M10 13.5C10 11.567 11.567 10 13.5 10h13C28.433 10 30 11.567 30 13.5v8c0 1.933-1.567 3.5-3.5 3.5H19l-5.2 4.2A1 1 0 0 1 12 28.4V25h-1.5C10.5 25 10 24.4 10 22.5v-9Z"
    fill="#ffffff"
  />
  <circle cx="15.5" cy="17.5" r="1.8" fill="#6d4ae6" />
  <circle cx="20" cy="17.5" r="1.8" fill="#ff7ab6" />
  <circle cx="24.5" cy="17.5" r="1.8" fill="#6d4ae6" />
</svg>
